            <ArticleTitle>Coronary thrombosis postpartum in a young woman with Still's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young woman with Still's disease sustained a small myocardial infarction 12 weeks after the delivery of a healthy male infant. This pregnancy was complicated by late onset proteinuric hypertension. Coronary angiography nine days after infarction revealed intracoronary thrombus which had resolved by 3 months with antithrombotic therapy. The angiographic appearances at 3 months suggested that a local vasculitis may have been the precipitating cause.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
